title: SSE relay finalized the response on the first chunk -- streaming was broken
  end to end
updated: 2026-08-08T05:03:49Z
---

Found by bench/ (fakellm + llmbench), not by the suite: streaming through Skeid returned correct headers, a 200 and an empty body, then logged "Transaction already destroyed" for every later chunk.

Two independent causes, both fatal:

1. The relay called $c->write($bytes) per chunk with no drain callback. A dynamic Mojolicious response is finished once its write queue empties, so the response ended after the first chunk. Fixed by queueing chunks and draining via write_chunk with a drain callback, finishing only once the queue is empty and upstream is done.

2. The first read event fires with an EMPTY chunk as soon as upstream headers are parsed, and writing an empty chunk finalizes the response. Fixed by skipping empty chunks.

Also fixed while in there: SSE frames were parsed per read, so a frame split across two reads was dropped -- usually the final one, which is the one carrying usage. Now buffered and parsed line by line.

Regression test: t/23-proxy-stream.t (real upstream, real socket, chunk-level client). Verified to fail against the old relay. The empty-chunk half is not reproducible through a Mojolicious upstream; it is covered by bench/ against fakellm.
